A clinic.

A priority is one of urgent, soon or routine.

A patient has a name (text), an age (a whole number) and a fever (a number).

The priority of a patient (a patient) is a priority:
urgent if its fever is at least 39.5,
soon if its fever is at least 38 or its age is more than 75,
otherwise routine.

The urgent names in a queue (a list of patients) is a list of texts:
its name for each patient in the queue where the priority of the patient is urgent.

Suppose ana is a patient with name "Ana", age 30 and fever 40.0.
Suppose bo is a patient with name "Bo", age 80 and fever 36.6.
Suppose cy is a patient with name "Cy", age 20 and fever 37.0.
For example, the priority of ana is urgent.
For example, the priority of bo is soon.
For example, the priority of cy is routine.
For example, the urgent names in a list of ana, bo and cy joined with "," is "Ana".
